"Through Toxicosis Markus can barely cast; he bluffs Randall that he still can."
"Serena, unseen, froze Markus's tea for him to sell the bluff to Randall."
"Markus's bond to Drathok is a facsimile, no true soul contract: he may speak of it freely."
"Drathok cannot sense Markus breaking terms, nor make him tell what he said to others."
"If Drathok dies, Markus's contract passes to Drathok's master Elasar, not into freedom."
"Drathok lied that a god bought Markus out; Elasar ordered Markus cut off from the gods."
"Randall offers to kill Drathok for Markus's contract, though it may mean war with Thiron demons."
"Randall also offers a Toxicosis cure, wealth, fame, craftsmen, acolytes to drain, clock rewinding."
"Randall wants Markus to face his Divine Arm again, to help Randall become a person again."
"Markus hides his true strength in bouts and builds power in secret for a break-out."
"Some of Markus's kills below were failed summons; it shook him, and he vows no needless deaths."
"The giant cores answered Markus's question with pulses: they want to fight the place that made them."
"Markus can speak to the system aloud and have it filter and answer; few know the system listens."
"A-Grade Divine Mana sits in his navel and will not budge; he could loose it all at once."
"Serena once fogged his memories of Elasar; they are restored now."
"Elasar appraised Markus, gasped, and wants him for a pawn; Elasar fears gods would weaponise him."
"Serena's quest to kill Elasar pays over two hundred Faith points."
"Through the moon tattoo Markus can call Serena, and she knows when he is in danger."
"A Faith wish from Serena could be a miracle of fair size, a Toxicosis cure among them."
"Markus left a Detonate charge in Abrah's chest as a leash and promised to take it out."
"Markus and the boar-man smith share a scheme to sell swords powered by Spirit-filled stones."
"Behind an iron gate in the vine cavern below, a hoard of chests waits that Markus has not reached."
"Markus has a true aspiration he tells no one."
"The Randall trial broke Markus's mind for a while; a figment of Serena talked him out of the cane."
"Markus's inborn trait can draw out essence; Randall thinks it could take youth, memory, even souls."
